cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SURD, please cite the paper below (preferred-citation). If you use surd.states, please also cite the Communications Physics paper under references."
type: software
title: "SURD: Synergistic-Unique-Redundant Decomposition of causality"
version: 1.3.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.13647182"
date-released: 2026-10-30
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ALD-Lab/SURD"
url: "https://github.com/ALD-Lab/SURD"
abstract: >-
  Python package that measures the information that past observations of a
  set of variables carry about the future of a target variable and decomposes
  it into redundant, unique and synergistic contributions, together with the
  causality leak from unobserved variables. The subpackage surd.states
  resolves the decomposition over the states of the variables.
keywords:
  - causality
  - causal inference
  - causality by states
  - information theory
  - synergy
  - redundancy
  - time series
